# Hardware component preferences

## Prefer SMD

Choose surface-mount parts wherever a part exists in both forms. Only fall back to
through-hole or a pre-built module when no surface-mount option exists — currently just
the ESP32-C3 SuperMini and the bench regulator module, both of which are replaced with
SMD equivalents on the custom PCB.

## Do not design around hand-soldering limits

**Hot air and a preheat/reflow plate are available.** Fine-pitch and bottom-terminated
packages are fully in scope: DFN, QFN, SOT-563, 0603, 0402. Pick the package that is
right for the circuit — size, thermals, parasitics, availability, price — not the one
that is easiest to reach with an iron.

## Reliability over unit cost

This is a permanent install intended to last many years, wired into shared building
infrastructure. Choose the part that lasts, not the cheapest that works: genuine
manufacturers over clones, **AEC-Q / automotive grade where it costs cents more**,
105 C >=5000 h capacitors from named brands, and generous voltage derating (aim 3x on
ceramics). Prefer X7R to X5R.

Do not propose a cheap prototype followed by a reliable rebuild. Prototype the
**topology and firmware**, not the component grade — cheap parts make bring-up harder
because a flaky part is indistinguishable from a design error. Split on form factor
instead: perfboard first, then PCB, with the same good components migrating across.

## Where the sweet spot is

**0805 for passives** is the default: comfortable to place and rework, no real downside
at this scale. Go smaller only when it buys something concrete, such as fitting a
regulator's input loop tightly or a bootstrap cap close to the pins.

## Suggest a package, not just a part number

Component recommendations must name the package explicitly, because most of these ICs
ship in four or five. Say `AP63203WU-7` in TSOT-23-6, or `SN74LVC1G07DBVR` in SOT-23-5,
not just "an AP63203".

## Verify against the datasheet

Before quoting a pinout, coil resistance, voltage limit or recommended passive value,
fetch the datasheet. Several earlier figures in this project were wrong from memory —
the G6K coil resistance, its maximum-voltage rating, and the 74LVC1G07 pin order all
had to be corrected. State explicitly when a value is unverified.
